Z||000000||FieroPerformance||11-16-2001||05:01 PM||||Here are some pictures that I just got back of my engine while I was rebuilding it. Right now it is back in the car and will be running in a few days     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/engine_back_rockers1.jpg">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/engine_top_pistons1.jpg">   <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/engine_side_pistons1.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/engine_top_rockers1.jpg">   <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/engine_side_heads1.jpg">   <P>Just thought some people might like to see them. Thanks for the space Cliff!<P>-Charlie<P>-----------------<P><BR>[This message has been edited by FieroPerformance (edited 11-16-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by FieroPerformance (edited 11-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||My7Fieros||11-16-2001||05:37 PM||||Kewl beans. Im gonna rebuild the 4 banger in my Indy, and have done some older carbed V8s...Ive always been kinda scared to rebuild the 6 cyl Fiero engine. They're so complicated w/ what seems to be miles and mazes of vaccuum lines...afraid it just would never run right afterwords. What all did you do? Curious.....<BR>BTW did you end up painting your block and heads?<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My7logo_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroPerformance||11-16-2001||06:37 PM||||Yeah, its not easy to figure all that stuff out, I took a lot of pictures before I took it apart so I could look at them to get it back together (VERY glad I did, I've used them a lot so far).<P>The block and heads are painted in the picture with a silver/gray colored paint.<P>This is a breakdown of what I did / had done:<BR>The block, heads (with valve job and some exhaust porting), crank and connecting rods were reconditioned.<BR>I put in slightly higher compression power forged pistons with plasma molly rings<BR>Crane compucam 2030 cam<BR>New:<BR>Push rods<BR>rocker arms<BR>seals and gaskets<BR>bearings<BR>valve springs<BR>water pump<BR>oil pump and filter screen<BR>head bolts<BR>New heavy duty clutch, pressure plate, and t/o bearing kit for my 5 speed Isuzu transmission<P><BR>I think that's most of it. So far I've spent about $2,000 on the parts and machine work. (I bought the car for $1,900 last year)<P>Let me know if you have any other questions.<P>-Charlie<P><BR>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsigfperformance.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by FieroPerformance (edited 11-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||11-16-2001||07:19 PM||||Where have you been going for machine work? Shop names and street in particular?||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroPerformance||11-16-2001||07:26 PM||||It is called Huck's Machine Shop. I will find his business card and email you all of the info (address, phone, ect.) Its off Route 32 somewhere around Mt. Carmel Tabasco Road.<P>It is owned and operated by 1 guy. I am VERY satisfied with the job he did and would recomend him to anyone looking for quality machine work. He also hooked me up with some really good prices on the other parts.<P>-Charlie||||reg||1
Z||000005||fiero56||11-16-2001||08:37 PM||||Well, my final shipment was waiting at my door tonight when I got home. All major pieces are now here with me.<BR>Pistons, rockers,pushrods, clutch set, etc arrived today. Complete cam set etc arrived this week. I will hopefully be able to post completed photos of mine in a month or two. This is a complete overhaul with everything replaced with new except for crank, rods, block and heads. Many will think I am nuts putting so much into an engine, when I could spend less for one that will put out similar power thats already rebuilt. But, I would rather do the work myself and put in much better pieces. Once its all broken in, it will be scheduled for a few dyno runs this spring.||||reg||1
